[38;2;124;124;124m\operatorname{div}: L^2(\Omega;\mathbb{R}^n) \to L^2(\Omega)$. The graph of a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mclosed operator from a separable space to a separable space is a closed subspace[0m[38;2;124;124;124mof a separable space, hence separable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mMore precisely, consider the map $T: H(\operatorname{div};\Omega) \to [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mL^2(\Omega;\mathbb{R}^n) \times L^2(\Omega)$ defined by $T(v) = (v, [0m
