[38;2;124;124;124m\operatorname{div}$ is a closed operator). $T$ is an isometric embedding (up to [0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe norm equivalence). Since $L^2(\Omega;\mathbb{R}^n) \times L^2(\Omega)$ is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mseparable (product of separable spaces), and the graph is a closed subspace, the[0m[38;2;124;124;124mgraph is separable. Therefore $H(\operatorname{div};\Omega)$ is separable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $H(\operatorname{div};\Omega)$ is a separable Hilbert space, it has an [0m
[38;2;124;124;124morthonormal basis (countable), which serves as a Schauder basis.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the answer is: Yes, $H(\operatorname{div};\Omega)$ has a Schauder basis.[0m

